{
  "name": "zander",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/fish/zander.py): a zander (pike-perch), 65 cm -- long and slender (its depth a fifth of its length), a long pointed head, the wide gape reaching back behind the eye, a pair of FANGS at the front of each jaw (`horn`s), the big GLASSY eye (milky silver: the tapetum of a twilight hunter); two dorsal fins close together, the first SPINY (notched between its spines), both and the tail speckled in rows of dark spots; 8 diffuse dark SADDLE bars on a grey-green back over silver-white flanks; the lower fins pale grey-yellow; small rowed scales, the lateral line painted. Each fin is one membrane sheet. A SWIMMER (the fish's plumbing).",
